---
# Checks tuned for the two-layer GDExtension / Drogon service split
# described in docs/conventions.adoc: the pure-logic core carries most of
# the correctness burden, so bugprone/performance/portability checks are
# on at full strength; readability checks are on but not fatal on their
# own (they don't block `just check` unless promoted via WarningsAsErrors).
# On the disabled checks: the first four are noise for this kind of service.
# The last two are disabled because they are WRONG here, not merely noisy —
# both were measured against shuffle_up's relay, the first TekAdept service to
# run clang-tidy at all.
#
# `portability-avoid-pragma-once` wants include guards instead of `#pragma
# once`. Every project-owned header at TekAdept uses `#pragma once` — 73 of 73
# across six services — as does Drogon itself, and every compiler these
# services target supports it. "Fixing" this would convert working, consistent
# headers to a more verbose idiom nothing here uses.
#
# `readability-convert-member-functions-to-static` produced 34 findings on that
# relay, and acting on ANY of them is harmful:
#
#   - On Drogon controllers the handlers are bound by member-function pointer
#     (`ADD_METHOD_TO(FallbackController::serveRoot, "/", Get)`). Making them
#     static would break routing.
#   - On the plain classes it flagged methods that demonstrably use non-static
#     members — `createTable` takes `std::lock_guard` on the instance's
#     `mutex_` and mutates `tables_`. Those cannot be static at all.
#
# Running `clang-tidy --fix` for this check did not merely produce bad advice:
# it emitted `static` on the out-of-class definitions in the .cpp files, which
# is invalid C++, and broke the build with "'static' can only be specified
# inside the class definition".
#
# `cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access` fires on every
# `Json::Value` object construction — `response["type"] = "table_created";` —
# which is JsonCpp's only idiom for creating a key. All 73 findings on
# shuffle_up's relay were of this form. There is no bounds-safe alternative:
# `.at()` THROWS when a key is absent, which is precisely the case when you are
# inserting one. Any Drogon service that builds JSON responses will hit this,
# so it is disabled estate-wide rather than suppressed per call site.
#
# CAVEAT, and it matters: this check is correct about `std::map::operator[]`,
# which silently default-inserts on a missing key. Disabling it hides that too.
# shuffle_up's MetricsController had exactly one such case — a `/proc/meminfo`
# lookup that reported 0 for absent fields instead of flagging them — found by
# this check before it was disabled, and fixed separately. When writing map
# lookups, reach for `.find()`/`.count()` deliberately; the linter is no longer
# watching.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  google-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  -readability-convert-member-functions-to-static,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access

WarningsAsErrors: >
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  performance-*

# Which headers clang-tidy reports on.
#
# This MUST match the project's actual source roots, and TekAdept services do
# not share one layout:
#
#   shuffle_up/server    src/
#   fitcards/server      src/, tests/
#   icebreaker/server    controllers/, models/, services/, config/
#   randoeats/bff        controllers/, services/  (no src/ at all)
#
# The previous value here was '(src|include)/.*', which matches nothing on
# half of those — and a header filter that matches nothing produces a clean
# run, not an error. That is the worst failure mode a lint config has.
#
# The alternation below covers every layout in use. Note this is POSIX ERE via
# llvm::Regex: there is NO lookahead, so dependency trees cannot be excluded by
# negation inside this pattern.
HeaderFilterRegex: '(src|include|controllers|models|services|filters|config|tests)/.*'

# Excluding dependency headers needs its own key, and it is NOT optional.
#
# Passing clang-tidy an explicit list of the project's own source files is not
# enough: that controls which translation units are analyzed, not which headers
# produce diagnostics. A .cpp of ours that includes a fetched header still
# reports findings from inside it. Measured on shuffle_up's relay before this
# key existed: 472 findings, of which 267 came from _deps/sentry-src — and one
# of those was promoted to an error by WarningsAsErrors below, so `analyze`
# could never pass no matter what the project's own code looked like.
#
# Requires clang-tidy 19 or newer (--exclude-header-filter).
ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(_deps|build|build-[^/]*|node_modules|\.cache)/.*'

FormatStyle: file

CheckOptions:
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.ClassCase
    value: CamelCase
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.FunctionCase
    value: camelBack
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.VariableCase
    value: camelBack
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberSuffix
    value: _
  - key: readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceCase
    value: lower_case
...
